declare(strict_types=1);

/**
 * Returns the sum of each row of a 2D array as a new 1D array.
 *
 * @param  array<int, array<int, int>> $matrix
 * @return array<int, int>
 */
function sumRows(array $matrix): array
{
    $sums = [];

    foreach ($matrix as $row) {
        $sums[] = array_sum($row);
    }

    return $sums;
}
```

## Shorter equivalent

Since `array_sum()` works on any array, `array_map()` does the whole job in one line:

```php
